      },
      "lineNbr": 855,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121198
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-12T22:55:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. In other words, we will set default\u003dTEMP_UNSUPPORTED when there is a built-in eSIM which is inactive and we are not able to get the EID (because we are on HAL 1.2-1.3).\n\nI can change the if condition to (mHasBuiltInEuicc \u0026\u0026 !anyEuiccIsActive \u0026\u0026 !isDefaultEuiccCardIdSet) and remove the hasEuicc check",
      "parentUuid": "6ab66449_5151bbe8",
